==Battleground==
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 16 seconds<sup>480f</sup>, delay 7~12.67 seconds<sup>210f~380f</sup>.
*5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 25.67 seconds<sup>770f</sup>, delay 9~13.33 seconds<sup>270f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kory]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 7~14 seconds<sup>210f~420f</sup>.
**1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns.
**2 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns.
**2 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.
**2 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The goal here is to outlast Kory's protection. Kory is a devastating unit here that makes quick work of your meatshields, while Duche and Shadow Boxer K rush in and wipe out your backup. Neither Duche nor Shadow Boxer K have a lot of hp, and as such, a couple hits from [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamet]] or any other rusher should put them out of commission. While meatshielding is key for the start of the level, due to the presense of Kory, you'll need to balance out damagers and meatshields by stopping the spam of meatshields so any incoming damagers can do their job and get rid of the Shadow Boxer K without the Kory waves.

